\tag{fdip}
\taxon{Discussion}
\title{Multiplication must bring the coefficients together}
\date{2026-11-17}

\p{A scalar vertex value can multiply a matter value in the
same fiber. For a cochain on an edge, a second factor may
instead be based at the other end of that edge, as in the
cubical product of \ref{fdip-00OX}. Which transport brings the two
values into a common fiber, and in which module should their
product lie when the coefficient module has no multiplication?}
